First released as a[ novel] written by the[ genius] author, N[agu]ib Mahfouz, scripted into a movie by Mahmoud El-Laithy, and directed by[ Hussein] Kamal, it tells the story of how frustrated, depressed, or utterly ap[athetic] Egyptians were after the huge[ setback] of the[ 1967] War. The story is full of imagery and symbolism, depicting history through the lives of seemingly[ irrelevant] people in the Egyptian population.
